<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:p1="clr-namespace:;assembly=Extensions"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:orcl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Control;assembly=OpenRigs.Control"
                 xmlns:lv="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.LiveView;assembly=OpenRigs.LiveView"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Description>The behaviour boxes' preflight, run from app-rig-control's Preflight page and card as the test mouse: the boxes' rig list (OpenRigs.Devices BBoxHardware) opens and readies every device as the box task does, no experiment folder (NoExperimentFolder), and the lab's check (OpenRigs.Devices PreflightChecks) counts each rig.yml device from its piece's data (the rig list's taps, OpenRigs.Devices BBoxHardwareTaps) and, from Go, writes the raw rows to RawFile with the questions of TaskPath (config\task-bbox.yml). A device that fails as it opens stops the preflight naming it, as it stops the task. Pulse and Reset on BehaviorBoard-Main are the board's ManualPulses piece. coen_qc_preflight_rig.judge applies the thresholds.</Description>
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="ConfigRoot" Description="The folder holding &lt;RIG&gt;\rig.yml, read by ReadLabRig; a launch property. LiveView keeps its own ConfigRoot: an edge into it makes Bonsai build it before the pieces, and it then streams nothing." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:ReadLabRig.bonsai">
        <Description>This machine's rig.yml (ConfigRoot\&lt;RIG&gt;\rig.yml) read once into the lab rig model: RigConfigs, RigFile and ConfigRoot, which every device piece reads. First, before anything that reads them.</Description>
        <ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</ConfigRoot>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:NoExperimentFolder.bonsai">
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="SubjectId" />
        <Property Name="SessionId" />
        <Property Name="LaunchId" Description="The launcher's run id; the launch's own, from app-rig-control." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Initialization</Name>
        <Description>The experiment controller (OpenRigs.Control, ExperimentControl, TCP 5561 on this machine), with no commands of its own: Pulse and Reset are the board's ManualPulses' and Confirm is PreflightChecks'. EndAfterStop ends headless Bonsai when it is still running 2 s after the controller's stop.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="SubjectId" />
              <Property Name="SessionId" />
              <Property Name="LaunchId" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Control:ExperimentControl.bonsai">
              <SubjectId />
              <SessionId />
              <LaunchId />
              <ControlEndpoint>@tcp://127.0.0.1:5561</ControlEndpoint>
              <Parameters />
              <Commands />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Description>Ends headless Bonsai when it is still running 2 s after the controller's stop: the live view's publisher threads keep the process alive until every device's teardown reaches them, and one held up kept Bonsai running until the agent's kill 30 s after End Testing (GREEN-DOME-2, 15 Nov 2026). Nothing in the editor.</Description>
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:EndAfterStop">
                <orcl:GraceSeconds>2</orcl:GraceSeconds>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Hardware</Name>
        <Description>The behaviour boxes' rig list (OpenRigs.Devices BBoxHardware), as in the box task: each piece from its rig.yml entry, opened and readied, Ready from its ReadyGate; and the board's ManualPulses (Pulse and Reset).</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BBoxHardware.bonsai" />
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:ManualPulses.bonsai">
              <Board>BehaviorBoard-Main</Board>
              <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges />
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="RawFile" Description="Where the raw rows go; a launch property." />
        <Property Name="TaskPath" Description="The task file app-rig-control writes at Go: config\task-bbox.yml with the form's edits." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:PreflightChecks.bonsai">
        <RawFile>preflight-raw.csv</RawFile>
        <TaskPath>..\config\task-bbox.yml</TaskPath>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BBoxHardwareTaps.bonsai" />
      <Expression xsi:type="lv:StreamDevices">
        <Name>LiveView</Name>
        <Description>Streams every rig.yml device the pieces publish (their &lt;Device&gt;.Data) to app-rig-control's live view (OpenRigs.LiveView): data on TCP 5556, video on 5558. No experiment folder, so the session key stays ready. Last in the workflow: it finds only subjects built before it.</Description>
        <lv:ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</lv:ConfigRoot>
        <lv:DataPort>5556</lv:DataPort>
        <lv:VideoPort>5558</lv:VideoPort>
      </Expression>
    </Nodes>
    <Edges>
      <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
    </Edges>
  </Workflow>
</WorkflowBuilder>
